silience, weather assessment. Weaknesses: interpersonal (nasty remarks), memory for numbers (could affect calculations). Communication? Not mentioned but nasty remarks suggests poor crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas. Strengths: situational awareness, technical cognition, leadership. Weaknesses: attitude (show-off, not open), could affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weaknesses: hot temper, know-it-all attitude (cooperation issues).\n\nWe need best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate balances? Candidate B has strong reliability and stress handling, but interpersonal issues severe (nasty remarks). That likely disqualifies for crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate A has egocentric, poor communication, not willing to learn \u2013 also problematic.\n\nCandidate C has leadership and situational awareness, but not open to new ideas, show-off \u2013 could affect crew.\n\nCandidate D has hot temper, know-it-all \u2013 also crew issues.\n\nWhich is least concerning? Maybe Candidate D: hot temper could be serious under stress, but he takes responsibility seriously, concentrates, solves problems. However hot temper could affect calmness under pressure.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates danger, sees complex connections, leadership, but attitude issues.\n\nWe might need more info about crew cooperation for each. Could ask other agents about crew cooperation observations. But we need to make a first contribution. Perhaps we can propose a provisional recommendation for Candidate C, noting strengths in situational awareness and leadership, but acknowledging concerns about openness. Or we could ask for more info about interpersonal behavior.\n\nGiven we must give a recommendation now, we can state provisional vote for Candidate C, with reasoning, and note need to discuss concerns.\n\nLet's craft message: \"I think Candidate C currently looks strongest because of anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, leadership, which are critical for long-distance flights. However concerns about being a show-off and not open to new ideas may affect crew cooperation. I propose we consider C as leading candidate, but we should compare with D's problem solving and responsibility.\"\n\nVote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
